/","Inherited from Middle High German ge-, from Old High German ga-, gi-, from Proto-West Germanic *ga-, from Proto-Germanic *ga-, from Proto-Indo-European *ḱóm.\nCognate with Low German ge-, e-, je- (Ermländisch), Yiddish גע־ (ge-), Dutch ge-, Old English ġe- (obsolete English y-, i-, a-), Gothic 𐌲𐌰- (ga-).\nThe umlaut in the collective nouns formed with this affix reflects the presence of the collective suffix *-ją at the Proto-Germanic level."]],"senses":[[5436,"ge-","prefix","Forms collective nouns, almost always neuter gender. Whenever possible, the root vowel is modified as well.",0],[5437,"ge-","prefix","Forms action nouns, usually with a sense of repetition or continuation. All of these nouns are neuter and have no plural.",1],[5438,"ge-","prefix","Forms nomina rei actae (Grammar Latin for “names of things done”, meaning verbal nouns that refer to the result of an action. In German, always of neuter gender).",2],[5439,"ge-","prefix","Forms past participles in combination with a suffix -en or -(e)t. Nouns are frequently made from the past participle.",3],[5440,"ge-","prefix","Forms verbs with terminative aktionsart. This is hardly productive after Early New High German and outside of dialects.",4],[5441,"ge-","prefix","Indicates association or togetherness; co-; fellow.",5]]},"haltbareres":{"entries":[["haltbareres",null,null,null]],"senses":[[228379,"haltbareres","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative neuter singular comparative degree of haltbar",0]],"inflections":[["haltbareres","haltbar","comparative,neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"hervorhübest":{"entries":[["hervorhübest",null,null,null]],"senses":[[124179,"hervorhübest","verb","second-person singular dependent subjunctive II of hervorheben",0]],"inflections":[["hervorhübest","hervorheben","archaic,formal,rare,second-person,singular,subjunctive,subjunctive-ii,subordinate-clause"]]},"indezentere":{"entries":[["indezentere",null,null,null]],"senses":[[475892,"indezentere","adj","i